            "title": "Authorization decision: guard clauses vs ternary operators",
            "description": "The same resource-authorization decision in three distinct control-flow forms: carrier A uses early-return guard clauses (pristine), carrier B re-expresses the same logic using nested ternary operators with early-return semantics, carrier C uses the cf_guard_nested nested-conditional form. All three are behaviorally identical via equivalence_test.php. No two carriers share a token run long enough for token/line tools to pair them, so only AST-canonicalizing and semantic detectors are expected to recover the cluster.",
